275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The aim of this project is to analyze a possible way to stabilize the unicycle robot, bringing it to the origin, when subject to actuator saturation. In particular, a discrete-time sliding mode controller is designed based on the discrete-time chained form of the unicycle model. The majority of applications of this robot considers the controller to be continuous, then once applied it is discretized and implemented through sample and hold devices. In general, this leads to poor performances, if the sampling period and frequency are not chosen small. Finally, two alternative controllers, continuous in nature since it is computed by a continuous time system, are proposed, in order to finally compare the two approaches.)
/E (The aim of this project is to analyze a possible way to stabilize the unicycle robot, bringing it to the origin, when subject to actuator saturation. In particular, a discrete-time sliding mode controller is designed based on the discrete-time chained form of the unicycle model. The majority of applications of this robot considers the controller to be continuous, then once applied it is discretized and implemented through sample and hold devices. In general, this leads to poor performances, if the sampling period and frequency are not chosen small. Finally, two alternative controllers, continuous in nature since it is computed by a continuous time system, are proposed, in order to finally compare the two approaches.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
