767 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 939 0 R
/E (The sliding mode controller is quite fast, even considering a large sampling period. The tuning is easy, due to the computations on the convergence parameters in closed form. It does not suffer of sampling frequency problems, so it is consistent in a physical application. The disturbance is rejected by a new computation of the convergence parameters.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
768 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 940 0 R
/E (The Polar Coordinates controller is slow but it could be improved by a more accurate tuning, but the singularity needs to be taken into account. Finally, the unicycle needs to point the desired cartesian position due to the definition of the error, this leads to a greater execution time.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
769 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 941 0 R
/E (The Feedback Linearization is as fast as the sliding mode controller, but its computational cost is higher. The matrix that needs to be inverted is a trigonometric one. The integrator increases the computational cost and execution time. Tuning is not easy, since it needs to be done accordingly to the developed conditions. Finally, the matrix is not invertible when the linear velocity is zero.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
